WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:11.136
Long time no see. Jeong Jinman.

2
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.721
Q.

4
00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.976
Unfortunately. the operation
that you've all been a part of

5
00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.852
will be temporarily suspended.

6
00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.188
Suspended?

7
00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:04.481
What are you talking about?

8
00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.775
Even after losing J and X?

9
00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.611
Then…

10
00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.532
what about Jeong Jinman?

11
00:01:14.241 --> 00:01:15.909
It's an order from the higher-ups.

12
00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:18.537
Securing the server is our priority.

13
00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:21.331
Babylon doesn't care if Jinman dies.

14
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.378
Priority?

15
00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.841
It's best if you go back to Japan.

16
00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:33.594
We need to send J back home as well.

17
00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:56.908
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

18
00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:03.832
EPISODE 05
NEGOTIATION

19
00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:05.667
{\an8}<i>Woojin. hey!</i>

20
00:02:05.751 --> 00:02:08.837
{\an8}<i>Don't close your eyes! No. you can't!</i>

21
00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:45.874
Miss Arin? You're awake now.

22
00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:49.544
I'm not Miss Arin.

23
00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:52.255
What?

24
00:02:52.964 --> 00:02:54.257
It's Jian.

25
00:02:58.637 --> 00:02:59.680
Jeong Jian.

26
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.349
Uh…

27
00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:07.354
The doctor on duty will be here
in 30 minutes.

28
00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:16.405
Uh. please don't get up. Jian.

29
00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.797
This is your new ID.

30
00:03:39.428 --> 00:03:42.722
- We've created a new identity for you.
- What about my uncle?

31
00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.644
I'm pretty sure he was in my room earlier.

32
00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.772
You're right.
He was here a few minutes before you woke.

33
00:03:50.856 --> 00:03:52.774
But he had to take care of something.
so he left.

34
00:03:57.612 --> 00:03:59.531
SOCIAL SECURITY CARD
LEE YENA

35
00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.702
I don't need the ID card.

36
00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:07.747
Changing identities is
kind of useless anyway.

37
00:04:09.124 --> 00:04:12.085
I'll just stay Jeong Jian.

38
00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:19.968
I know you're still processing.

39
00:04:20.051 --> 00:04:22.012
but we've put together
a statement for you.

40
00:04:22.596 --> 00:04:24.848
The boat had been docked at the pier.

41
00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:28.477
Then Mr. Woojin brought you along
for the maintenance and inspection.

42
00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.937
We were out at sea
when the boat broke down.

43
00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:34.441
The reef punctured the boat.

44
00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:38.612
The ship started sinking
because water rushed in.

45
00:04:41.239 --> 00:04:43.617
I put on the life jacket
that was on board.

46
00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:46.328
But Woojin…

47
00:04:48.914 --> 00:04:51.416
<i>thought he could save us
by fixing the engine.</i>

48
00:04:53.418 --> 00:04:56.797
<i>His leg got caught
in the damaged wheelhouse.</i>

49
00:04:57.714 --> 00:04:59.758
<i>He was dragged down with the boat.</i>

50
00:05:03.762 --> 00:05:06.515
I lost… consciousness.

51
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.101
I woke up in the hospital.

52
00:05:10.852 --> 00:05:12.938
All right. that's all for now.

53
00:05:13.939 --> 00:05:15.732
You can go. you must be exhausted.

54
00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:20.946
Poor Woojin.
I can't believe this happened.

55
00:05:24.491 --> 00:05:26.827
It's fortunate that it was
successful there in Thailand at least.

56
00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:29.538
For now. take the recovered items and…

57
00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.339
Take the recovered item
and return to Korea.

58
00:05:42.717 --> 00:05:47.931
Honestly. people in this country
have no basic manners.

59
00:05:51.643 --> 00:05:52.727
What's going on?

60
00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:54.020
Uh…

61
00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.441
It's. uh…

62
00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:02.571
<i>Black Mountain Alliance has received
organized support for years</i>

63
00:06:02.654 --> 00:06:05.532
<i>from a private military company
named Babylon.</i>

64
00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:08.326
<i>Clashes between militant
factions are now spreading</i>

65
00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.120
<i>into neighboring regions.</i>

66
00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.038
<i>- Authorities are treating…</i>
- That's not. uh…

67
00:06:12.706 --> 00:06:13.832
That's not all.

68
00:06:14.666 --> 00:06:18.003
<i>The assassinations of the high-ranking
government officials have escalated.</i>

69
00:06:19.462 --> 00:06:21.423
<i>According to sources.
there is a possibility</i>

70
00:06:21.506 --> 00:06:23.675
<i>that this was a strategic operation.</i>

71
00:06:23.758 --> 00:06:25.927
<i>The evidence is leading
to a private organization...</i>

72
00:06:26.011 --> 00:06:27.971
<i>We are joined today
by an expert in the field.</i>

73
00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:30.849
{\an8}<i>The weapons North Korea unveiled
at the Victory Day parade</i>

74
00:06:30.932 --> 00:06:32.559
{\an8}<i>have been significantly upgraded.</i>

75
00:06:33.351 --> 00:06:34.603
Jeong Jinman.

76
00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:40.692
That disgusting parasite.

77
00:07:33.578 --> 00:07:34.579
Arin.

78
00:07:59.854 --> 00:08:00.855
Arin…

79
00:08:02.774 --> 00:08:04.651
are you blaming yourself?

80
00:08:11.199 --> 00:08:14.828
Most of the aunties here
have lost their husbands

81
00:08:14.911 --> 00:08:17.372
because something
happened to them out at sea.

82
00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.084
They see it as their fate.

83
00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:24.003
It's life.

84
00:08:24.087 --> 00:08:25.213
I'm sorry.

85
00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.342
Auntie. really. I'm sorry.

86
00:08:31.177 --> 00:08:32.679
I'm sorry.

87
00:08:32.762 --> 00:08:34.556
I'm sorry.

88
00:08:34.639 --> 00:08:36.766
I'm sorry. Auntie.

89
00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:39.060
So sorry.

90
00:08:48.862 --> 00:08:50.155
Listen well.

91
00:08:50.238 --> 00:08:54.409
You're blaming yourself.
but it won't bring Woojin back.

92
00:08:55.326 --> 00:08:58.413
You need to keep living your own life.
Understand?

93
00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:03.418
I know it's hard right now.
but when you look back.

94
00:09:03.501 --> 00:09:06.921
you'll see that
this is just a moment in your life.

95
00:09:08.048 --> 00:09:09.174
You must be brave.

96
00:09:09.716 --> 00:09:12.218
Make sure to live tenaciously and be bold.

97
00:09:12.927 --> 00:09:15.472
You'll heal Arin by living a good life.

98
00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:29.360
We're all right.

99
00:09:31.279 --> 00:09:32.405
Don't worry about us here.

100
00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:34.991
Just live.

101
00:09:36.659 --> 00:09:37.702
Arin. go.

102
00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:40.872
Forget about us.

103
00:09:42.874 --> 00:09:44.250
Live your life.

104
00:10:02.185 --> 00:10:03.478
You'll be all right alone?

105
00:10:09.109 --> 00:10:10.318
We'll come back tomorrow.

106
00:10:57.282 --> 00:10:58.324
Now…

107
00:11:01.369 --> 00:11:03.121
I'm all alone.

108
00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:52.212
<i>Jeong Jinman…</i>

109
00:11:54.631 --> 00:11:56.633
<i>this is the darkness you created.</i>

110
00:11:59.427 --> 00:12:01.095
<i>I will make you pay for it.</i>

111
00:12:13.942 --> 00:12:16.819
You and your brother.
you've always been good kids.

112
00:12:17.987 --> 00:12:21.282
From when he was this tall
and you were this tall.

113
00:12:22.825 --> 00:12:23.868
I'm in your debt.

114
00:12:24.702 --> 00:12:26.829
Sir. thank you for the past few days.

115
00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:31.584
Ichika…

116
00:12:33.461 --> 00:12:36.589
reach out to me anytime you need.

117
00:12:40.969 --> 00:12:42.178
I appreciate it.

118
00:12:48.059 --> 00:12:49.269
Thank you so much.

119
00:12:50.937 --> 00:12:51.938
Be strong.

120
00:13:14.544 --> 00:13:16.129
Is M still in Thailand?

121
00:13:16.879 --> 00:13:18.840
He's back in Korea with the asset.

122
00:13:20.591 --> 00:13:23.052
- He apologized for not being here.
- Yeah.

123
00:13:26.347 --> 00:13:28.057
Thank you for being here.

124
00:13:28.141 --> 00:13:29.309
So what now?

125
00:13:33.104 --> 00:13:34.856
Let's go back to Korea.

126
00:13:37.984 --> 00:13:41.029
I'm going to murder Jeong Jinman
with my own hands.

127
00:14:16.522 --> 00:14:18.649
Hey. you're gonna
have to wait. okay?

128
00:14:31.704 --> 00:14:33.164
Thank you. Thank you so much.

129
00:14:56.729 --> 00:15:00.358
Boss. a lot of orders
from the Philippines are coming in.

130
00:15:00.691 --> 00:15:01.692
Hm?

131
00:15:03.444 --> 00:15:04.445
Oh!

132
00:15:11.202 --> 00:15:12.328
Jeong Jian!

133
00:15:24.924 --> 00:15:26.092
When did you move in?

134
00:15:26.259 --> 00:15:29.345
Uh… We've been preparing this whole time.

135
00:15:29.428 --> 00:15:32.682
but it's only been about ten days
since we settled in.

136
00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:50.783
I'll carry it.

137
00:15:50.867 --> 00:15:53.119
- I've got it.
- Okay.

138
00:16:07.133 --> 00:16:10.344
I'm really glad that
you didn't get hurt. Jeong Jian.

139
00:16:11.512 --> 00:16:14.640
Jeong Jinman is… here. right?

140
00:16:15.892 --> 00:16:20.855
Mm-hmm. The boss was really
worried about you.

141
00:17:05.233 --> 00:17:06.567
You're okay. right?

142
00:17:08.694 --> 00:17:09.946
So glad you're here.

143
00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.239
This will be your room for the time being.

144
00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:57.743
Oh. great. No windows for me.

145
00:17:58.661 --> 00:18:01.414
Yeah. Obviously. It's a basement.

146
00:18:07.878 --> 00:18:11.507
Take some time to rest.
You're probably exhausted.

147
00:18:17.305 --> 00:18:18.973
I tried to decorate it like our old place.

148
00:18:19.056 --> 00:18:20.558
It reminds me of that day.

149
00:18:23.311 --> 00:18:24.979
It's not exactly the same. right?

150
00:18:25.646 --> 00:18:27.231
No cameras in my room this time?

151
00:18:34.405 --> 00:18:35.698
You made the right choice.

152
00:18:37.533 --> 00:18:39.827
Thanks for coming back. Jeong Jian.

153
00:18:41.912 --> 00:18:43.789
I didn't come back to make you happy.

154
00:19:09.523 --> 00:19:11.067
You scared me.

155
00:19:13.569 --> 00:19:14.779
You should stop.

156
00:19:15.946 --> 00:19:18.240
Boss. I said. we shouldn't put
a camera in there.

157
00:19:18.324 --> 00:19:19.367
Wait a sec.

158
00:19:20.368 --> 00:19:24.830
That camera was already installed there.
You decided to make that Jian's room.

159
00:19:24.914 --> 00:19:26.666
That's not important.

160
00:19:26.749 --> 00:19:29.418
Don't think about continuing
to spy on her.

161
00:19:29.502 --> 00:19:32.922
- Hey. Look. Do me a favor.
- Huh?

162
00:19:33.881 --> 00:19:36.258
Get rid of it before she notices.

163
00:19:37.343 --> 00:19:39.512
- This guy…
- Thanks.

164
00:20:41.449 --> 00:20:45.953
<i>This information
leak cost about 20 billion dollars.</i>

165
00:20:46.036 --> 00:20:48.748
<i>What will happen if they find out</i>

166
00:20:48.831 --> 00:20:52.418
<i>we supplied the weapons
to both the government and the rebels?</i>

167
00:20:54.545 --> 00:20:58.382
<i>The rebels aren't the problem right now.
What do you think North Korea would do?</i>

168
00:20:58.466 --> 00:21:00.926
<i>The US government won't just sit back
and do nothing.</i>

169
00:21:01.719 --> 00:21:05.848
The Korean branch dropped the ball.
I'm here to recover it.

170
00:21:05.931 --> 00:21:07.016
<i>Nonsense!</i>

171
00:21:07.099 --> 00:21:08.684
<i>Take some responsibility!</i>

172
00:21:09.393 --> 00:21:10.895
<i>However…</i>

173
00:21:10.978 --> 00:21:14.023
<i>didn't this highly confidential
information become public</i>

174
00:21:14.106 --> 00:21:16.025
<i>because your operation failed?</i>

175
00:21:16.108 --> 00:21:19.904
The operation failure
was entirely my responsibility.

176
00:21:21.071 --> 00:21:23.741
<i>Good job. everyone.
I'll take it from here.</i>

177
00:21:27.244 --> 00:21:29.413
<i>You were careless
and moved impulsively.</i>

178
00:21:29.497 --> 00:21:31.665
<i>Did you stop to think about
what will happen</i>

179
00:21:31.749 --> 00:21:35.252
<i>if Jeong Jinman decides to leak
other confidential information?</i>

180
00:21:37.546 --> 00:21:39.131
I apologize for my actions.

181
00:21:39.215 --> 00:21:41.592
{\an8}<i>Do you think that I can't see through you?</i>

182
00:21:42.384 --> 00:21:43.969
{\an8}<i>Your self-interest is clear.</i>

183
00:21:44.637 --> 00:21:49.892
{\an8}<i>You're planning to use the murthehelp app
to conduct your own business. are you not?</i>

184
00:21:50.434 --> 00:21:54.355
I'm not. sir. I only have
Babylon's best interests in mind.

185
00:21:54.438 --> 00:21:58.150
<i>I understand. I've read the report too.</i>

186
00:21:58.234 --> 00:22:01.403
<i>I get that it's
a very attractive business model.</i>

187
00:22:02.404 --> 00:22:04.865
<i>But that should not be our first priority.</i>

188
00:22:05.324 --> 00:22:06.325
<i>Correct?</i>

189
00:22:07.868 --> 00:22:11.038
{\an8}<i>We have no interest
in that cockroach Jeong Jinman.</i>

190
00:22:11.121 --> 00:22:14.333
{\an8}<i>Whether you decide to kill him
or buy him. do what you please.</i>

191
00:22:14.416 --> 00:22:16.418
{\an8}<i>We need you to prioritize.</i>

192
00:22:16.502 --> 00:22:18.504
<i>You are to retrieve the server first.</i>

193
00:22:18.587 --> 00:22:20.381
Your message is received.

194
00:22:20.464 --> 00:22:24.301
<i>Regarding the murthehelp system.
I will leave it to your discretion</i>

195
00:22:24.385 --> 00:22:27.137
<i>on how to take over and move forward
with the business.</i>

196
00:22:28.055 --> 00:22:32.893
{\an8}<i>If you are successful. I will entrust
the entirety of Babylon Korea to you.</i>

197
00:22:41.151 --> 00:22:44.029
She's staying in a hotel
that's not very far from Babylon.

198
00:22:45.573 --> 00:22:49.285
Since it's just a regular hotel.
it should be fairly easy to gain access.

199
00:22:52.663 --> 00:22:55.082
I guarantee
it won't be as easy as you think.

200
00:22:55.165 --> 00:22:57.501
We will have breakfast together.

201
00:22:57.585 --> 00:23:01.839
And depart at eight o'clock sharp tomorrow
to begin our sightseeing schedule.

202
00:23:01.922 --> 00:23:05.259
Depart at eight o'clock. Understood!

203
00:23:05.342 --> 00:23:11.098
That's all for today's schedule
and you can rest in your rooms.

204
00:23:13.267 --> 00:23:17.396
The convenience store is
on the first floor

205
00:23:17.479 --> 00:23:19.690
and you can use it freely. anytime.

206
00:23:38.584 --> 00:23:39.627
Why are you up here?

207
00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:42.880
Huh? Where's everybody?

208
00:23:42.963 --> 00:23:45.174
Strange. Did I get off on the wrong floor?

209
00:23:45.257 --> 00:23:48.052
This floor is fully booked
for conference participants only.

210
00:23:49.803 --> 00:23:50.804
Really?

211
00:23:50.888 --> 00:23:51.889
I'm sorry?

212
00:23:52.473 --> 00:23:54.475
It's nothing. Nothing.
I didn't understand.

213
00:23:54.558 --> 00:23:58.103
Oh. it's okay.
Wow. but you're really tall. aren't you?

214
00:23:59.104 --> 00:24:00.272
What's going on?

215
00:24:00.356 --> 00:24:02.399
A Chinese tourist came up here by mistake.

216
00:24:09.657 --> 00:24:11.241
It looks like that woman
and her little sidekick

217
00:24:11.325 --> 00:24:12.910
are staying on the same floor.

218
00:24:13.994 --> 00:24:15.663
Should I eliminate them when I can?

219
00:24:16.997 --> 00:24:18.666
I can probably do it pretty easily.

220
00:24:20.709 --> 00:24:21.752
No. thanks.

221
00:24:22.962 --> 00:24:26.924
Even if you eliminate them. Babylon will
just keep sending their replacements.

222
00:24:27.007 --> 00:24:28.801
Do you know her?

223
00:24:29.843 --> 00:24:32.096
When I was in the special forces.

224
00:24:32.179 --> 00:24:34.932
we had an operation to rescue hostages
in Southeast Asia.

225
00:24:35.015 --> 00:24:36.850
That's the only time we've met.

226
00:24:37.601 --> 00:24:40.562
There were Koreans
amongst the Japanese hostages.

227
00:24:40.646 --> 00:24:43.607
Since Japan couldn't deploy troops.
Babylon was called in.

228
00:24:44.650 --> 00:24:46.902
You said. in Hanam-do.
the Babylon team leader was

229
00:24:46.986 --> 00:24:48.070
a Japanese woman. right?

230
00:24:52.116 --> 00:24:55.411
If memory serves correct.
her code name is Q.

231
00:24:59.915 --> 00:25:03.043
Cheolseung.
look into the team leader and Q.

232
00:25:03.127 --> 00:25:05.838
and include all of their team members
that entered Korea.

233
00:25:05.921 --> 00:25:07.840
Get all the detailed information you can.

234
00:25:08.674 --> 00:25:09.883
<i>I'm Q.</i>

235
00:25:09.967 --> 00:25:12.511
The next time we meet.
we'll go have a drink together.

236
00:25:12.594 --> 00:25:14.013
Thank you.

237
00:25:14.096 --> 00:25:16.432
Long time no see. Jeong Jinman.

238
00:25:28.610 --> 00:25:29.653
ATTORNEY JANG INSEOP

239
00:25:29.737 --> 00:25:32.156
"Negotiation requested."

240
00:25:32.281 --> 00:25:35.617
Those dumb assholes always have
to fuck around and find out the hard way.

241
00:25:35.701 --> 00:25:37.202
We can't do this now.

242
00:25:37.286 --> 00:25:39.038
We don't have enough manpower.

243
00:25:39.121 --> 00:25:41.165
Code Yellow took heavy losses
on Hanam-do Island.

244
00:25:41.248 --> 00:25:42.958
Our Code Reds are scattered.

245
00:25:43.042 --> 00:25:45.169
They're waiting to see what happens.

246
00:25:46.795 --> 00:25:50.049
Right. it could be dangerous.
It's not time to negotiate.

247
00:25:50.132 --> 00:25:53.052
Let's secure a safe house first.
And then we can move Jian.

248
00:25:53.135 --> 00:25:54.762
Am I some kind of object?

249
00:25:55.637 --> 00:25:57.431
Move me wherever you want?

250
00:25:59.183 --> 00:26:00.851
Over and over.

251
00:26:00.934 --> 00:26:02.478
Without ever negotiating.

252
00:26:05.022 --> 00:26:06.982
You hide. then fight and move.

253
00:26:07.066 --> 00:26:09.902
You repeat the cycle again and again.
And then what?

254
00:26:10.486 --> 00:26:12.738
How many people are gonna die
to protect me?

255
00:26:14.114 --> 00:26:18.202
Do you even know
how many people on Hanam-do Island died?

256
00:26:22.289 --> 00:26:25.918
When Uncle Jinwoo dies
and Minhye <i>Eonni</i> dies. does this end?

257
00:26:27.252 --> 00:26:28.712
I won't accept that.

258
00:26:28.796 --> 00:26:31.423
I'm not allowing any of you
to sacrifice yourselves.

259
00:26:33.133 --> 00:26:34.218
Do you understand?

260
00:26:38.097 --> 00:26:39.515
That's why I came back.

261
00:26:50.359 --> 00:26:53.904
All right. What's your plan. then?

262
00:26:54.655 --> 00:26:57.199
What are you going to do
to prevent all of us…

263
00:26:57.991 --> 00:26:59.243
from being sacrificed?

264
00:27:00.744 --> 00:27:01.995
Whatever I can.

265
00:27:07.292 --> 00:27:08.544
Listen up. Jeong Jian.

266
00:27:10.254 --> 00:27:12.756
It's not possible to negotiate
without strength.

267
00:27:13.632 --> 00:27:15.425
You can't just talk a big game.

268
00:27:15.509 --> 00:27:18.345
You better put your money
where your mouth is first.

269
00:27:18.428 --> 00:27:19.638
You need to prove it.

270
00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:22.224
Hm.

271
00:27:22.683 --> 00:27:23.725
I get it.

272
00:27:25.477 --> 00:27:26.603
I'll prove it to you.

273
00:27:28.438 --> 00:27:29.940
Tell me what to do. I'll do it.

274
00:27:45.873 --> 00:27:48.667
<i>The customer you have dialed
cannot answer your call.</i>

275
00:27:48.750 --> 00:27:50.711
<i>Please hang up and try the call again.</i>

276
00:27:54.965 --> 00:27:56.091
No umbrella?

277
00:27:58.010 --> 00:28:00.596
I forgot my umbrella all the time
when I was little.

278
00:28:07.978 --> 00:28:10.314
See this? Do you want one?

279
00:28:13.901 --> 00:28:14.943
Try them on.

280
00:28:20.198 --> 00:28:23.368
It's all right. You can trust me.

281
00:28:24.536 --> 00:28:25.996
I'm friends with your father.

282
00:28:30.042 --> 00:28:31.209
What?

283
00:28:31.293 --> 00:28:33.295
- Oh. no.
- Why are you so bad at this?

284
00:28:34.087 --> 00:28:36.256
Why are you so good at this?

285
00:28:36.340 --> 00:28:37.466
- You...
- Shoot!

286
00:28:39.551 --> 00:28:41.470
Oh. hey. It's my dad.

287
00:28:56.026 --> 00:28:58.528
- General Suho!
- Hi. Dad!

288
00:29:00.614 --> 00:29:02.157
Where did you get this raincoat?

289
00:29:03.659 --> 00:29:06.620
Your friend. She gave me an extra one.

290
00:29:07.079 --> 00:29:08.956
Hm? My friend?

291
00:29:14.419 --> 00:29:17.089
Mr. Lee Jaeyoon. It's good to see you.

292
00:29:19.049 --> 00:29:20.550
Oh. it's been a while.

293
00:29:20.634 --> 00:29:22.427
Good to see you too. Hey.

294
00:29:23.428 --> 00:29:25.263
Suho. jump in the car. wait for Dad.

295
00:29:26.264 --> 00:29:28.725
Thank you for the raincoat.
See you later.

296
00:29:28.809 --> 00:29:29.810
Bye.

297
00:29:48.996 --> 00:29:51.415
What do you want? Why are you here?

298
00:29:51.498 --> 00:29:54.376
- Jeong Jian.
- Speak louder.

299
00:29:55.377 --> 00:29:58.630
I'm Jeong Jian. Jeong Jinman's niece.

300
00:29:58.714 --> 00:30:01.508
Jeong Jian? Code Green?

301
00:30:06.763 --> 00:30:08.306
Did Jinman send you?

302
00:30:08.390 --> 00:30:12.352
That guy's a total scumbag.
He sent you after my son?

303
00:30:13.145 --> 00:30:15.689
It's pretty funny hearing
the word scumbag…

304
00:30:17.065 --> 00:30:19.067
- come out of your mouth.
- What?

305
00:30:23.613 --> 00:30:26.825
The day Mr. Kim betrayed us
and brought all the Code Reds to attack.

306
00:30:27.784 --> 00:30:29.161
Why weren't you there?

307
00:30:31.329 --> 00:30:33.123
Did Jinman send you
to confront me about this?

308
00:30:34.207 --> 00:30:35.208
No.

309
00:30:36.168 --> 00:30:39.087
I didn't come here
to argue with you. all right?

310
00:30:39.921 --> 00:30:41.339
I'm here for a reason.

311
00:30:41.423 --> 00:30:45.260
Only two people on this Earth can persuade
the Code Reds to move.

312
00:30:45.343 --> 00:30:48.096
My uncle said one of them was Mr. Kim.
but he's dead.

313
00:30:49.514 --> 00:30:50.724
That's why I'm here.

314
00:30:51.516 --> 00:30:53.977
The only other person is you.
Mr. Ahn Seongbeom.

315
00:30:55.270 --> 00:30:58.774
- Will you please persuade the Code Reds?
- Maybe you haven't heard.

316
00:31:00.317 --> 00:31:01.485
I'm retired.

317
00:31:02.903 --> 00:31:03.945
Wait.

318
00:31:05.572 --> 00:31:07.074
Aren't you even curious?

319
00:31:09.743 --> 00:31:11.203
I found your son.

320
00:31:12.079 --> 00:31:13.747
I knew who you were…

321
00:31:14.664 --> 00:31:16.374
and what your alias was.

322
00:31:19.044 --> 00:31:20.378
You know what's cool?

323
00:31:21.213 --> 00:31:25.342
I offered the Code Purples extra money
to give me info on you. but they declined.

324
00:31:25.425 --> 00:31:28.929
They said it's an unwritten rule.
Never touch family.

325
00:31:30.222 --> 00:31:32.974
Every one of them refused to say anything.

326
00:31:33.725 --> 00:31:37.187
So how do you think it is
that I found out who you were…

327
00:31:37.979 --> 00:31:40.190
and exactly where your son was?

328
00:31:48.406 --> 00:31:51.993
Babylon's been collecting
personal information on every Code Red.

329
00:31:52.077 --> 00:31:55.122
Those assholes put every single one
of you under surveillance.

330
00:31:56.081 --> 00:31:57.124
Why?

331
00:32:03.547 --> 00:32:04.714
Tell me why!

332
00:32:05.173 --> 00:32:07.801
I'm retired!
Why is Babylon digging up my information?

333
00:32:07.884 --> 00:32:09.469
Why do you think. huh?

334
00:32:10.345 --> 00:32:11.638
It's always about money.

335
00:32:11.721 --> 00:32:13.765
Babylon is a big corporation

336
00:32:13.849 --> 00:32:15.976
and they're trying to swallow murthehelp.
to take over.

337
00:32:16.852 --> 00:32:18.311
I'll be blunt with you.

338
00:32:19.104 --> 00:32:22.649
The Babylon division from Japan
came to take murthehelp from us.

339
00:32:23.567 --> 00:32:25.694
They've been trying to mobilize Code Reds.

340
00:32:26.319 --> 00:32:29.865
They've even created a fake app
and are recruiting people without codes.

341
00:32:32.159 --> 00:32:33.994
They'll probably start a war with us.

342
00:32:34.953 --> 00:32:36.621
We don't have enough manpower.

343
00:32:37.747 --> 00:32:38.790
We need your help.

344
00:32:44.629 --> 00:32:46.423
Jeong Jinman. you listening?

345
00:32:46.506 --> 00:32:47.841
<i>Your niece has guts.</i>

346
00:32:48.508 --> 00:32:51.469
<i>But if you ever try to send anyone
to my son again.</i>

347
00:32:51.553 --> 00:32:52.804
<i>I promise you.</i>

348
00:32:52.888 --> 00:32:56.766
<i>I'll have no problems tearing apart
and killing both you and your niece.</i>

349
00:32:56.850 --> 00:33:00.353
<i>The only reason I'm holding back now
is as a final courtesy to you</i>

350
00:33:00.437 --> 00:33:02.189
<i>as an old colleague of mine.</i>

351
00:33:16.786 --> 00:33:18.455
I think I messed it up.

352
00:33:19.873 --> 00:33:21.249
Please come and get me.

353
00:33:37.349 --> 00:33:40.685
You won't be able to change
Ahn Seongbeom's mind that easily.

354
00:33:40.769 --> 00:33:41.770
Don't give up yet.

355
00:33:43.313 --> 00:33:45.815
I didn't go to see his son
to threaten his family.

356
00:33:50.195 --> 00:33:51.780
It just backfired.

357
00:33:52.781 --> 00:33:53.949
Jian…

358
00:33:55.492 --> 00:33:57.369
you probably feel that

359
00:33:57.452 --> 00:34:00.956
your uncle really messed up your life
by involving you in all of this.

360
00:34:01.039 --> 00:34:02.707
But he really does care.

361
00:34:02.791 --> 00:34:05.835
And trust me. he understands
the pain of losing someone you love.

362
00:34:07.420 --> 00:34:10.632
Jinman's lost a lot of people
in every stage of his life.

363
00:34:10.715 --> 00:34:14.761
As a soldier. a mercenary.
and long after leaving Babylon.

364
00:34:16.596 --> 00:34:17.722
It's been hard.

365
00:34:19.224 --> 00:34:21.685
Jinman's experienced so much loss that…

366
00:34:22.394 --> 00:34:25.855
at some point he just accepted
this endless cycle of pain.

367
00:34:25.939 --> 00:34:28.608
That's why he's so guarded with everyone.

368
00:34:31.236 --> 00:34:33.989
Your uncle wanted you
to be strong and resilient.

369
00:34:34.739 --> 00:34:37.492
He just doesn't want you
to end up like he did.

370
00:34:38.535 --> 00:34:40.745
I don't want to end up like him either.

371
00:34:45.375 --> 00:34:47.502
I'm not going to do things like he did.

372
00:34:49.129 --> 00:34:50.130
Ever.

373
00:35:11.693 --> 00:35:13.486
I heard that you want to spar with me.

374
00:35:13.570 --> 00:35:15.238
Since Master Pasin's not here...

375
00:35:30.337 --> 00:35:33.840
Inventory check is the basics
of running the shopping mall.

376
00:35:34.924 --> 00:35:38.053
Finish all of this today
and make sure you get it inspected.

377
00:35:43.933 --> 00:35:45.352
This is 9 mm.

378
00:35:45.435 --> 00:35:47.312
This is 5.56.

379
00:35:47.395 --> 00:35:49.481
and this is 7.62.

380
00:35:49.564 --> 00:35:53.777
Simply put. the larger the caliber.
the more damage it does.

381
00:35:57.781 --> 00:35:59.824
A longer barrel
increases the range.

382
00:36:00.533 --> 00:36:03.495
When the sun's in front of you.
close the scope cover

383
00:36:04.371 --> 00:36:05.455
and look in the middle.

384
00:36:06.414 --> 00:36:08.958
Or you'll give yourself away
because of the sun's reflection.

385
00:36:10.168 --> 00:36:12.212
You can ask Brother
to give you a few of these.

386
00:36:19.344 --> 00:36:21.429
In order to prepare for hacker attacks.

387
00:36:21.513 --> 00:36:25.809
we maintain our security by switching
the site cover every 72 hours.

388
00:36:32.816 --> 00:36:34.984
Click the invisible button
under the event tag

389
00:36:35.068 --> 00:36:37.153
and it'll reveal the login
to the real site.

390
00:36:37.237 --> 00:36:39.531
When you log in
using the three biometric credentials

391
00:36:39.614 --> 00:36:42.992
that you originally registered with.
along with the code.

392
00:36:44.119 --> 00:36:46.705
you will get access
to the real murthehelp.

393
00:36:47.664 --> 00:36:50.041
What'd you do? Why'd you get denied?

394
00:36:50.667 --> 00:36:52.043
Poor circulation.

395
00:37:16.568 --> 00:37:17.861
No!

396
00:37:25.618 --> 00:37:27.328
You already finished dismantling it?

397
00:37:29.831 --> 00:37:32.917
This clover protected my life
when I escaped North Korea.

398
00:37:33.001 --> 00:37:34.461
It's yours now.

399
00:37:34.544 --> 00:37:35.879
You're giving it to me?

400
00:37:35.962 --> 00:37:39.340
My wishes all came true already.
I don't need it anymore.

401
00:37:43.678 --> 00:37:45.764
Thank you. as always. Director Kim.

402
00:37:46.681 --> 00:37:51.186
Let's begin the new company agreement
between Jaewon Co. Ltd. and murthehelp.

403
00:38:12.624 --> 00:38:13.917
This way. hurry.

404
00:38:21.549 --> 00:38:25.720
This place is a place only the boss
and I know about.

405
00:38:41.486 --> 00:38:44.489
Jeong Jian. listen well.

406
00:38:45.824 --> 00:38:51.079
This place is a secret passage
you can use to escape in an emergency.

407
00:38:51.162 --> 00:38:53.498
You have to go in about 300 meters.

408
00:38:53.581 --> 00:38:56.417
When you reach the 250-meter mark.

409
00:38:56.501 --> 00:38:58.753
you can slam
the blast door shut behind you.

410
00:38:59.838 --> 00:39:01.631
What's at the end of it?

411
00:39:01.714 --> 00:39:02.841
The exit?

412
00:39:02.924 --> 00:39:06.511
Oh. right. In front of it.
there's a small room.

413
00:39:06.594 --> 00:39:08.847
Like the old shopping mall.

414
00:39:08.930 --> 00:39:10.306
From there. you can just…

415
00:39:12.600 --> 00:39:14.936
burn the whole shopping mall down.

416
00:39:15.019 --> 00:39:16.896
- Why?
- Why?

417
00:39:16.980 --> 00:39:20.275
You're escaping through means
that it's an emergency situation

418
00:39:20.358 --> 00:39:22.485
and you can't leave any traces behind.

419
00:39:56.102 --> 00:39:57.353
<i>Eonni.</i>

420
00:39:59.022 --> 00:40:04.527
Do you think it's gonna be hard for me
to live a normal life like everybody else?

421
00:40:08.948 --> 00:40:09.949
<i>Jinman…</i>

422
00:40:11.743 --> 00:40:15.914
am I going to have a hard time living
a normal life like everyone else?

423
00:40:30.261 --> 00:40:33.890
You fucking bitch.
Who on Earth are you?

424
00:40:35.683 --> 00:40:36.726
You don't remember?

425
00:40:37.477 --> 00:40:41.522
I am the fucking bitch
that you sold for 100 dollars.

426
00:40:46.402 --> 00:40:47.403
<i>Yeah.</i>

427
00:40:49.197 --> 00:40:50.239
<i>Probably.</i>

428
00:40:51.366 --> 00:40:53.326
You won't be able
to live like everyone else.

429
00:40:53.993 --> 00:40:55.370
It's not possible. Jian.

430
00:40:58.998 --> 00:41:03.127
But… luckily.
your uncle is still alive and well.

431
00:41:05.630 --> 00:41:07.966
And there are people
who want to protect you.

432
00:41:09.717 --> 00:41:12.512
We eat meals together.
spend time together.

433
00:41:13.304 --> 00:41:14.764
Like you're doing with me right now.

434
00:41:17.558 --> 00:41:18.643
Maybe…

435
00:41:20.311 --> 00:41:21.729
this is our own kind of normal.

436
00:41:57.974 --> 00:42:00.601
- What is this?
- What do you mean. what is this?

437
00:42:00.685 --> 00:42:03.271
The enemy will take advantage
of your weakness.

438
00:42:03.354 --> 00:42:04.772
You gotta keep your head together.

439
00:42:26.544 --> 00:42:27.545
What?

440
00:42:28.212 --> 00:42:29.547
What are you doing here at this hour?

441
00:42:29.630 --> 00:42:33.092
Jian told me to come.
She called a meeting.

442
00:42:33.176 --> 00:42:34.177
What?

443
00:42:37.305 --> 00:42:38.473
Huh?

444
00:42:45.980 --> 00:42:47.440
Everyone is here.

445
00:42:51.527 --> 00:42:53.446
I gave things some serious thought.

446
00:42:54.655 --> 00:42:55.782
This man.

447
00:42:59.786 --> 00:43:02.872
- The server administrator?
- Yes.

448
00:43:02.955 --> 00:43:04.749
One of the prior administrators

449
00:43:04.832 --> 00:43:07.585
happened to be on the bus
that we ordered to be exploded.

450
00:43:07.668 --> 00:43:09.754
- So we hired a new one.
- Okay.

451
00:43:09.837 --> 00:43:12.548
- You vetted him thoroughly. right?
- Yes.

452
00:43:28.648 --> 00:43:30.525
Who was that man?

453
00:43:30.608 --> 00:43:32.985
Head of security
during Lee Yonghan's time here.

454
00:43:33.069 --> 00:43:34.362
Oh…

455
00:43:34.570 --> 00:43:38.157
He let Jeong Jinman get away.
lost the server. and yet here he is.

456
00:43:38.241 --> 00:43:39.492
I'll take care of it.

457
00:43:42.036 --> 00:43:43.412
What is it now?

458
00:43:47.750 --> 00:43:48.876
Negotiate?

459
00:43:56.843 --> 00:43:59.804
They made the offer first?

460
00:43:59.887 --> 00:44:01.597
Yes. No.

461
00:44:04.684 --> 00:44:05.935
Yes.

462
00:44:14.402 --> 00:44:16.821
What are you playing at. Jeong Jinman?

463
00:44:19.282 --> 00:44:20.950
So where are we doing this?

464
00:46:03.511 --> 00:46:05.012
Where is Jeong Jinman?

465
00:46:06.013 --> 00:46:07.473
Jeong Jinman's not coming.

466
00:46:15.648 --> 00:46:16.983
I'm Jeong Jian.

467
00:46:17.984 --> 00:46:20.236
I will be doing the negotiating.

468
00:46:24.365 --> 00:46:25.992
You're breaking your promise again.

469
00:46:26.701 --> 00:46:28.953
Do you think we're playing
some kind of game here?

470
00:46:31.497 --> 00:46:32.707
You are the one…

471
00:46:34.292 --> 00:46:35.793
playing games.

472
00:46:40.923 --> 00:46:43.718
Aren't you. Ms. Kusanagi?

473
00:46:50.808 --> 00:46:54.061
<i>The CEO came in person on our side.
It's uneven.</i>

474
00:46:56.314 --> 00:46:59.775
<i>The status level should match
in negotiation. but there is…</i>

475
00:47:00.484 --> 00:47:02.486
<i>a proxy instead of you.</i>

476
00:47:54.872 --> 00:47:56.290
<i>This is your last chance.</i>

477
00:47:57.750 --> 00:48:01.504
If you don't come with me.
your boyfriend will also die.

478
00:48:18.479 --> 00:48:19.855
You two have met before.

479
00:48:20.856 --> 00:48:23.109
You remember. don't you?

480
00:48:24.860 --> 00:48:26.987
In order to match my status level.

481
00:48:27.071 --> 00:48:30.157
Jeong Jinman would need to be
the one sitting in front of me.

482
00:48:30.241 --> 00:48:32.284
But it's fine.

483
00:48:32.368 --> 00:48:34.995
You and I are lucky
to live in today's world.

484
00:48:35.079 --> 00:48:38.541
a world where a young lady like you
can become a CEO.

485
00:48:40.376 --> 00:48:41.585
Like me.

486
00:48:58.894 --> 00:49:01.856
Ms. Kusanagi. I apologize

487
00:49:02.940 --> 00:49:06.318
for the damage caused to Babylon
over the past two years.

488
00:49:12.199 --> 00:49:13.534
I'll accept that.

489
00:49:13.617 --> 00:49:15.995
I'd hardly call that damage. though.

490
00:49:16.078 --> 00:49:18.998
It doesn't even scratch the surface
compared to what you've been through.

491
00:49:19.081 --> 00:49:21.208
You lost your parents when you were seven

492
00:49:21.292 --> 00:49:24.837
and found out what your uncle really did
for a living when you became an adult.

493
00:49:24.920 --> 00:49:27.882
Not to mention the day you survived
the carnage in your home.

494
00:49:29.425 --> 00:49:32.136
Do you remember when you shot the drone
with your slingshot?

495
00:49:32.219 --> 00:49:34.013
Hm.

496
00:49:34.513 --> 00:49:36.432
We were expecting to meet with Jinman.

497
00:49:36.515 --> 00:49:40.269
Our intention was to hold him responsible
for Babylon's losses.

498
00:49:41.061 --> 00:49:42.813
But his niece showed up instead.

499
00:49:43.481 --> 00:49:44.773
That's too bad.

500
00:49:44.857 --> 00:49:46.650
Well. I'm the one here.

501
00:49:48.152 --> 00:49:50.404
You're going to have to negotiate with me.

502
00:49:53.532 --> 00:49:55.284
Oh. yeah? Why would we do that?

503
00:49:55.367 --> 00:49:57.536
Starting this very minute.

504
00:49:57.620 --> 00:50:00.331
Jeong Jinman is no longer involved
with murthehelp.

505
00:50:00.414 --> 00:50:02.082
He's officially stepped down.

506
00:50:05.085 --> 00:50:07.213
This vicious cycle of fighting
will keep repeating

507
00:50:07.296 --> 00:50:09.256
as long as Jeong Jinman is involved.

508
00:50:09.340 --> 00:50:13.302
The problem is that his style of operation
always uses force with force.

509
00:50:16.388 --> 00:50:18.390
If the fighting never stops…

510
00:50:21.852 --> 00:50:23.771
both sides will continue to lose.

511
00:50:26.106 --> 00:50:28.359
I want us to coexist together.

512
00:50:28.442 --> 00:50:30.736
I'm proposing we form a partnership.

513
00:50:30.819 --> 00:50:33.489
Murthehelp and Babylon working together.

514
00:50:33.572 --> 00:50:35.032
As we hand over the server.

515
00:50:35.115 --> 00:50:38.202
we'll also be sharing
murthehelp's business with Babylon.

516
00:50:38.285 --> 00:50:39.370
You can stop…

517
00:50:43.958 --> 00:50:48.128
No need to bother making knock-offs.
like that half-baked app you made.

518
00:50:48.212 --> 00:50:51.674
Instead. we'll share the profits
and prioritize Babylon's weapons

519
00:50:51.757 --> 00:50:54.009
in our Sales and Distribution departments.

520
00:50:54.093 --> 00:50:56.428
Also. if over time.

521
00:50:57.221 --> 00:50:59.932
we feel that there's enough trust
built between us.

522
00:51:00.015 --> 00:51:04.603
we might even be open to the possibility
of selling murthehelp entirely to Babylon

523
00:51:04.687 --> 00:51:06.063
at a reasonable price.

524
00:51:07.106 --> 00:51:08.148
M and A.

525
00:51:09.191 --> 00:51:10.276
That sound good?

526
00:51:11.610 --> 00:51:12.695
<i>He says they haven't breached anything</i>

527
00:51:12.778 --> 00:51:13.862
<i>other than the exposed data.</i>

528
00:51:14.697 --> 00:51:16.615
They've only breached the exposed data.

529
00:51:20.911 --> 00:51:22.079
And your terms?

530
00:51:25.624 --> 00:51:26.625
They're simple.

531
00:51:27.626 --> 00:51:28.711
Jeong Jinman.

532
00:51:31.130 --> 00:51:33.257
Nobody's allowed to touch him from now on.

533
00:51:34.633 --> 00:51:39.680
In other words. you are asking us
to spare your uncle's life.

534
00:51:42.641 --> 00:51:43.976
In so many words.

535
00:51:50.024 --> 00:51:51.483
This is the key to the truck.

536
00:51:51.567 --> 00:51:55.571
If you pick it up. I'll consider it
as you accepting my offer.

537
00:51:55.654 --> 00:51:58.532
You're very bold
in begging for Jinman's life.

538
00:52:02.036 --> 00:52:06.081
If you brought me ten of Jinman's heads
wrapped in a tiny little bow.

539
00:52:06.165 --> 00:52:07.625
it still wouldn't be enough.

540
00:52:09.627 --> 00:52:10.711
If I refuse?

541
00:52:14.256 --> 00:52:15.466
Then…

542
00:52:18.385 --> 00:52:19.637
we'll all…

543
00:52:20.888 --> 00:52:21.972
die right here.

544
00:52:30.230 --> 00:52:31.774
See those bombs?

545
00:52:31.857 --> 00:52:33.942
They're linked to my biometric signal.

546
00:52:34.026 --> 00:52:35.736
The moment that signal's cut…

547
00:52:37.863 --> 00:52:38.947
…they'll detonate.

548
00:52:43.243 --> 00:52:44.870
Maybe it's because you're young.

549
00:52:45.663 --> 00:52:47.289
you're not afraid of dying.

550
00:52:49.124 --> 00:52:50.626
You're so reckless.

551
00:52:53.671 --> 00:52:54.713
Dying?

552
00:52:55.881 --> 00:52:57.883
I don't care about that anymore.

553
00:52:58.801 --> 00:53:00.302
I'm beyond that now.

554
00:53:02.763 --> 00:53:05.265
I already died once on that island.

555
00:53:10.229 --> 00:53:11.313
Are you scared?

556
00:53:16.985 --> 00:53:18.028
Let's hear it.

557
00:53:20.656 --> 00:53:21.740
Is dying…

558
00:53:23.742 --> 00:53:25.536
something you're afraid of?

559
00:53:27.996 --> 00:53:29.039
Lights!

560
00:53:32.251 --> 00:53:34.086
Switch to infrared now.

561
00:53:40.300 --> 00:53:41.927
I've long wondered

562
00:53:42.886 --> 00:53:46.473
how you survived
those impossible situations.

563
00:53:47.766 --> 00:53:51.437
Seeing you now. I finally understand.

564
00:54:03.115 --> 00:54:06.201
See you soon. Jeong Jian.

565
00:55:00.589 --> 00:55:03.217
- I appreciate it.
- Fuck that bullshit.

566
00:55:05.385 --> 00:55:08.388
Jeong Jinman.
I didn't come because I like you.

567
00:55:08.472 --> 00:55:10.933
I broke my promise to your niece
that one day.

568
00:55:11.767 --> 00:55:13.227
But now I've paid my debt.

569
00:55:14.895 --> 00:55:18.941
I'm done with murthehelp and code shit
and anything related to it.

570
00:55:20.108 --> 00:55:23.362
- Forget about me.
- I appreciate it. regardless.

571
00:55:25.489 --> 00:55:26.490
Let's go.

572
00:55:43.549 --> 00:55:46.051
When you shouted "Ms. Kusanagi."

573
00:55:46.134 --> 00:55:48.220
you scared the living hell out of me.

574
00:55:48.303 --> 00:55:50.097
When did I do that?

575
00:55:50.180 --> 00:55:52.182
Little Jian was so cool.

576
00:55:52.266 --> 00:55:54.226
She really has
grown into herself.

577
00:55:54.309 --> 00:55:56.395
Hey. how did you know
it was a camera?

578
00:55:56.478 --> 00:56:00.649
- I just looked and saw it.
- Oh. your bloodline is strong.

579
00:56:01.233 --> 00:56:03.402
Hurry up and eat. It's done.

580
00:56:03.485 --> 00:56:06.697
Don't eat it all!
Leave me some too!

581
00:56:06.780 --> 00:56:09.741
<i>Oh. man. our Brother is</i>
<i>a </i>samgyeopsal<i> killer. What a shame!</i>

582
00:56:09.825 --> 00:56:11.910
<i>Hey. just</i>
<i>stuff your face with </i>ramyeon.

583
00:56:11.994 --> 00:56:13.996
<i>- Challenge!
- Finish up there and come down.</i>

584
00:56:14.663 --> 00:56:16.248
They're rubbing it in.

585
00:56:17.040 --> 00:56:20.544
- Code Blue?
- Transport is really important.

586
00:56:20.627 --> 00:56:24.423
We have to deliver the products
to the target locations discreetly.

587
00:56:24.506 --> 00:56:26.925
but right now
each code handles them directly.

588
00:56:28.135 --> 00:56:31.430
By creating a new code
that specializes in transportation.

589
00:56:31.513 --> 00:56:34.766
I think it would really help us
down the line. don't you?

590
00:56:35.726 --> 00:56:36.852
What do you think?

591
00:56:39.688 --> 00:56:40.772
Why look at me?

592
00:56:41.773 --> 00:56:43.734
Murthehelp's CEO is Jeong Jian.

593
00:56:43.817 --> 00:56:47.112
If she says we should do it.
then we do it.

594
00:56:47.863 --> 00:56:49.448
Okay. Good.

595
00:56:49.531 --> 00:56:51.116
I'm Code Blue number one.

596
00:56:51.199 --> 00:56:53.368
I always fly the helicopter
or drive the car.

597
00:56:53.452 --> 00:56:55.662
- I handle all transportation. right?
- No.

598
00:56:55.746 --> 00:56:59.291
- Uncle Jinwoo. you can't be Code Blue.
- Why not?

599
00:56:59.374 --> 00:57:00.584
One more thing.

600
00:57:01.543 --> 00:57:03.670
I would like if all of us here…

601
00:57:06.089 --> 00:57:07.299
<i>Brother included.</i>

602
00:57:10.218 --> 00:57:11.928
Everybody at this table.

603
00:57:12.596 --> 00:57:16.725
becomes Code Green from now on.

604
00:57:18.602 --> 00:57:19.645
What?

605
00:57:22.022 --> 00:57:25.359
It's only natural. You're all important.

606
00:57:26.068 --> 00:57:27.861
We've all become like family now.

607
00:57:27.944 --> 00:57:29.946
It's only right that you're Code Green.

608
00:57:30.030 --> 00:57:33.867
That means that Uncle Jinwoo.
you're not Code Blue. You're Code Green.

609
00:57:35.702 --> 00:57:36.953
Minhye <i>Eonni.</i>

610
00:57:39.414 --> 00:57:41.041
Uncle Cheolseung. you too.

611
00:57:55.931 --> 00:57:57.641
This suddenly…

612
00:57:58.517 --> 00:58:02.020
reminds me of my mother
that I had to leave behind in North Korea.

613
00:58:04.439 --> 00:58:06.942
I haven't heard that word
since coming to the South.

614
00:58:08.193 --> 00:58:09.194
Family.

615
00:58:10.404 --> 00:58:11.863
Thank you. Jian.

616
00:58:14.616 --> 00:58:17.744
Hey. come on. Let's drink to that.
Yeah? Huh?

617
00:58:17.869 --> 00:58:19.371
- Okay. In one shot!
- Here.

618
00:58:20.580 --> 00:58:23.917
Our hearts to the motherland.
our livers to our comrades.

619
00:58:24.000 --> 00:58:25.794
- Cheers!
- Cans up.

620
00:58:25.877 --> 00:58:26.920
Cheers.

621
00:58:30.590 --> 00:58:33.552
<i>If we don't celebrate on
a day like today. when will we ever. huh?</i>

622
00:58:33.635 --> 00:58:35.846
<i>You're right. That's right. Wow!</i>

623
00:58:35.929 --> 00:58:37.639
<i>Comrade's saying
all the right things today.</i>

624
00:58:37.723 --> 00:58:39.307
- Hey. take a photo.
- Yeah. good idea.

625
00:58:40.475 --> 00:58:41.810
Pasin.

626
00:58:43.770 --> 00:58:46.523
<i>Help me. Jinman.</i>

627
00:58:46.606 --> 00:58:51.361
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

628
00:58:51.820 --> 00:58:53.071
<i>Jeong Jian…</i>

629
00:58:54.114 --> 00:58:55.824
That little kid was cute.

630
00:58:56.616 --> 00:58:59.453
She must have thought
I really went to negotiate.

631
00:59:09.087 --> 00:59:14.468
So. in return. you are going to have
to do a little work for us.

632
00:59:27.647 --> 00:59:29.107
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG

633
00:59:30.305 --> 01:00:30.657
